    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW29UPMDb4qUd72jyXpmdZhjY)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent, based on current `main` (#522).\n- Depends on: nothing; it only adds a module, a doc, a test and three keys.\n- If merged first: nothing breaks.\n- Conflicts with: any open PR that also edits the `require` list of `sp-academic.org` or the `L b f` keys of `sp-keys.org` (adjacent hunks, keep both sides). I did not compare file lists with the open PRs one by one.\n- Branch name: it is `claude/project-thread-euuy1u`, not `NNN-...`; I cannot rename a branch of an open PR from here. Rename it on GitHub (Branches, rename) to `<this PR number>-biblatex-converter` if you want the prefix.\n- No `CHANGELOG.org` edit, as agreed; the nightly tidy picks it up.\n\n## Summary\n\n- New module `sp-bibtex-biblatex` (literate doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-bibtex-biblatex.org`) renames BibTeX-only fields to BibLaTeX names and writes accents as Unicode.\n  - `journal` to `journaltitle`, `address` and `place` to `location`, `school` to `institution`, `archiveprefix` and `primaryclass` to the `eprint` names.\n  - `@electronic` and `@webpage` become `@online`.\n  - `f{\\\"u}r` becomes `für`; protective braces, `\\&`, `\\%`, `\\_` stay.\n  - A name whose BibLaTeX twin exists with another text is left and reported.\n- Never changed: dates (you chose to keep `year` and `month`), citekeys, `file` fields, `url`, `doi`. Citekeys and PDF names stay ASCII; the report lists the 11 keys and 284 `file` fields with non-ASCII characters on a copy of your library.\n- Safety: dry-run report first (`C-; L b f L`), one question, backup per run, `C-; L b f r` restores. A binary file with a `.bib` name (`epistemologie.bib` is a macOS alias) and non-UTF-8 files are skipped. The result must have the same keys in the same order or nothing is written.\n- Keys: `C-; L b f l` convert, `L` report, `r` restore.\n- Findings are in `docs/architecture/biblatex-and-typst.org`:\n  - your exports use CSL (citeproc), not biber, so no document needs BibTeX-only features;\n  - `bibtex-mode` handles BibLaTeX with the `biblatex` dialect (already set); it lacks `@video`, `@review`, `@standard`, `@audio`, which the converter adds while it works;\n  - Typst reads `.bib` as BibLaTeX through Hayagriva and accepts `journal`/`journaltitle`, `address`/`location`, `school`/`institution` and `date` or `year`+`month`, but not `place` or `@webpage`;\n  - `org-cite-export-processors` has no `typst` entry, so a Typst export uses citeproc text, not `#cite`; a one-line follow-up, not changed here.\n\n## Checked by Claude\n\n- 11 ERT tests in `tests/sp-bibtex-biblatex-test.el` and the `sp-keys` tests pass (Emacs 29.3, headless).\n- Dry run on a copy of the library (80 files, 12 seconds): 6645 entries change, 4246 `journal`, 1524 `place`, 1193 with accents, 103 `school`, 88 `address`, 78 `@webpage`; 3 `@electronic`; no entry lost; one file skipped. Nothing was run on the real library.\n- Not run: Typst compile, Emacs 31, the interactive commands in a GUI.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `C-; L b f L` (dry run, all files): a report buffer opens; counts are about those above; `epistemologie.bib` is listed as skipped; no file changes (`git -C ~/Documents/bibliography status` is clean) (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `C-u C-; L b f L` on one small file: only that file is reported (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] The report lists the non-ASCII citekeys and `file` names and the `date` values with a time, without changing them (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `C-; L b f l` on one file (`C-u`), answer no: nothing is written. Run again, answer yes: a backup folder is reported and `git diff` shows only field renames and accents (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `C-; L b f r` restores that file byte for byte (`git diff` empty) (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Full run on all files; `citar-refresh`; open a few entries in citar: titles with accents show as Unicode, journals show (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Compile a small Typst file with `#bibliography(\"converted.bib\")` and cite an article, a thesis and an `@online`: journal, place and accents appear, and `\\&` shows `&` rather than a backslash (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Regression: `C-; L b f d` (date fix) and `C-; L b f o` (field order) still open their reports (untested by Claude)\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (and `git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/project-thread-euuy1u`; the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) so the config matches main again.\n- If you ran the conversion on the library: `C-; L b f r` restores the files from the run's backup folder, or `git -C ~/Documents/bibliography restore .` since the library is under git.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCxFkKhzC6rHZfA9ea)_",
